                    131.0,
                    804.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- Force safety is the decisive interaction constraint. Only the force-constrained predictive interaction-dynamics controller achieves both accurate tracking (0.03 mm) and the 0.5 N bound (peak 0.47 N). Classical impedance (0.17 N) and joint-space PD (no contact) stay under the bound only by being too soft to track the penetrating target—safety bought with accuracy, the trade the constraint removes.",
            "block_bbox": [
                111,
                805,
                604,
                996
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    111.0,
                    805.0
                ],
                [
                    604.0,
                    805.0
                ],
                [
                    604.0,
                    996.0
                ],
                [
                    111.0,
                    996.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "• Offset-free motion regulation without a force limit overshoots the bound. The unconstrained predictive controller, driving hard to eliminate position error against the penetrating target, pushes the contact force to 0.60N (0.595N precisely)—19% over  $ F_{safe} $. This is far milder than the multi-newton overshoot a stiff lumped plant predicts (the compliant catheter and 8N tendon cap the realizable force below 1N), but the bound is still breached: offset-free motion regulation and force safety remain in tension, resolved only by the hard interaction constraint (0.60→0.47N at identical tracking).",
            "block_bbox": [
                110,
                997,
                603,
                1259
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    110.0,
                    997.0
                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    997.0
                ],
                [
                    603.0,
                    1259.0
